1
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:15,030
This is really neat!

2
00:00:15,030 --> 00:00:17,810
When do we eat?

3
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:20,490
First, we have to catch some fish.

4
00:00:20,490 --> 00:00:27,720
In order to catch fish, you have to do this.

5
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:29,210
Here we go.

6
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:34,490
That's it.

7
00:00:34,490 --> 00:00:37,230
Then drop it into the water.

8
00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:41,220
All of this comes before eating. OK?

9
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:43,880
How do you know so much about fishing?

10
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:45,720
Grandpa taught me.

11
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:48,630
We spent a lot of time fishing together.

12
00:00:48,630 --> 00:00:58,700
Now, the important thing is to get the hook close to the fish.

13
00:00:58,700 --> 00:00:59,690
All right?

14
00:00:59,690 --> 00:01:08,750
Like this.

15
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:10,990
I think I see some fish right under us, Dad.

16
00:01:10,990 --> 00:01:12,960
Oh, not a chance!

17
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:15,660
I just saw a big one!

18
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:16,640
Hi, there!

19
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:17,590
Hi.

20
00:01:17,590 --> 00:01:18,290
What's your name?

21
00:01:18,290 --> 00:01:19,690
Albert.

22
00:01:19,690 --> 00:01:20,650
Are you all alone?

23
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:22,490
Yes, sir.

24
00:01:22,490 --> 00:01:23,990
How old are you, Albert?

25
00:01:23,990 --> 00:01:27,560
I'm ten.

26
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:29,120
Where's your father?

27
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:33,790
He's up there at the lodge.

28
00:01:33,790 --> 00:01:35,290
Does he know you're here?

29
00:01:35,290 --> 00:01:37,030
Yes, sir.

30
00:01:37,030 --> 00:01:40,220
OK, Robbie, maybe you should watch him.

31
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:42,130
The water's pretty deep here.

32
00:01:42,130 --> 00:01:50,730
I'll watch him, Dad.

33
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:52,580
What time is it?

34
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:56,220
It's almost lunchtime, and no fish yet.

35
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,950
I can go up to the lodge for some hot dogs and drinks.

36
00:01:58,950 --> 00:02:00,170
No way!

37
00:02:00,170 --> 00:02:02,520
We're here to catch our lunch.

38
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:06,650
To catch fish, you need the right magic.

39
00:02:06,650 --> 00:02:07,470
That's right.

40
00:02:07,470 --> 00:02:08,060
I forgot!

41
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:09,780
The right magic.

42
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:11,450
Do it for Robbie, Dad.

43
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:12,380
You remember?

44
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:13,580
Sure. Come on.

45
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:18,560
Well, first, you have to turn your hat around like this.

46
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:23,460
Then you close your eyes and say the magic words.

47
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:32,360
Fish, fish, send me a fish.

48
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:39,360
Fish, fish, send me a fish.... I got one!

49
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:41,360
See, it works!

50
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,460
It's a big one!

51
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:45,220
Well, it always worked for me, too.

52
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:55,390
Grandpa, get the net, please!

53
00:02:55,390 --> 00:02:56,910
Dad, you got one, too!

54
00:02:56,910 --> 00:02:58,200
You bet I have!

55
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:04,570
Easy, Philip, easy.

56
00:03:04,570 --> 00:03:07,600
Sorry, Dad.

57
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:13,310
Well, one more and I've got a pair of boots.

58
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:15,180
You didn't say the magic words.

59
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:16,590
Robbie's right.

60
00:03:16,590 --> 00:03:19,430
Yes, but you did, and we've got our lunch.

61
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:20,950
Let's build a fire and cook it!

62
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:23,390
Come on, Albert, you can help us!

63
00:03:23,390 --> 00:03:25,150
I want to stay here and fish.

64
00:03:25,150 --> 00:03:38,000
All right, but be careful.

65
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,180
Is it finished yet?

66
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:40,120
I think so.

67
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:44,420
I hope you like your fish well done.

68
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:46,380
Burned, you mean.

69
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:58,490
Hey, I'm a doctor, not a chef.

70
00:03:58,490 --> 00:04:01,790
Help! Help! I can't swim!

71
00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:04,990
Dad! Grandpa! He fell in!

72
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:06,520
Easy does it, Robbie.

73
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:22,510
That a boy.

74
00:04:22,510 --> 00:04:26,000
That's it.

75
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,430
He's not breathing, Philip!

76
00:04:27,430 --> 00:04:29,340
Robbie, run to the car!

77
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:30,520
Bring a blanket and my medical bag.

78
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,570
Yes, Dad.

79
00:04:32,570 --> 00:04:43,680
Now, come on, son. Come on, son.

80
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:46,680
Breathe, Albert!
